I do not run it as such.  But installed on various occasions for folks
with required licenses.  We used for that 3.2 libraries.  4.0 stuff is
using some system calls which were not emulated in 2.0 kernels.  Kernels
from 2.2 series expanded this emulated list but I did not have a reason,
or opportunity, to check if this enough for Maple and 4.0 libraries.

BTW - you have to make sure that CONFIG_MATHEMU is set in your kernel
configuration or plotting in Maple will bomb out immediately.  Such
configuration creates problems for em86 and any kernel above 2.2.11.  So
far you can take a contents arch/alpha/math-emu/ from 2.2.11 and drop
that in into 2.2.13, say, and you will get a working kernel.  It is not
clear, at least to me, what went haywire.

