"David Hocking" <davidh@student.unsw.edu.au> writes:

> Hi, I'm fairly new to linux and have finally got Debian loaded
> ok. Although when i try to run startx it tells me that /dev/mouse
> isn't a file or directory.

First you have to make sure that the mouse port is found by the kernel
you are running. Check out 'dmesg'.

> So can anyone tell me how you load a mouse driver or something so
> that /dev/mouse is "mounted" (or loaded).

Then you need to create symbolic link so that '/dev/mouse' points to
your actual mouse device. For example 'ln -s /dev/ttyS1 /dev/mouse' to
use mouse on serial port 1 and 'ln -s /dev/psaux /dev/mouse' to use
PS/2 mouse port.

