Alexander Verhaar wrote:
> 
> Maybe this is a typical newbie question, but I never saw/notice the
> following question.
> 
> What precisely is an "Unalligned error"?
> I'm normally only programming on the x86 platform, and
> just begun to program on my Alpha.

It means that data is not at the proper places in memory

The Alpha is a 64 bit machine and therefore expects it's data to be
properly stored in memory.
It is unaligned is 
(address of data) mod sizeof(type) != 0  where sizeof(type) is 1,2,4 or
8

With glibc 2.1, timespec contains 64 bit values, when before it had 32
bit values. This made ping generate 'unaligned traps' because the values
were not at a 8 byte boundary

- Alex



