  Well, the CPU is not the problem with running the DEC 3000's.  It's
the bus and interrupts that are different.  They use TurboChannel, and
are quite strange.  A DEC 3000/X is a 21064 Alpha CPU at 166-300mhz
IIRC.
  However, I looked up the 3300, and it's a Digital AlphaServer, which
is a totally different beast.  Your box should be PCI/EISA and should
run linux.  Make sure you get the EISA config utility for it.  There
should be a copy somewhere on ftp.digital.com.  Try looking at:
http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/archive/3300/digitalserver3300.html
  Any Alpha that can run NT should be able to run Linux as well.  

