We've no trouble with the same card in some 433 MHz PWSs (running
RedHat 5.1).  I presume you're using XFree?  Check your
/etc/X11/XF86Config (or whatever the Debian equivalent is).  Do you
have a Monitor section with good HorizSync and VertRefresh ranges?
With some reasonable Modelines?

Example sections (for a DEC 21" monitor - don't just copy, check your
manual for HorizSync and VertRefresh):


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Section "Monitor"

    Identifier  "DEC PCXBV-KA/KB"
    VendorName  "Unknown"
    ModelName   "Unknown"

    HorizSync   30.0-95.0
    VertRefresh 50-152

# 1280x1024 @ 76 Hz, 81.13 kHz hsync
Modeline "1280x1024"  135    1280 1312 1416 1664  1024 1027 1030 1064

EndSection


Section "Device"
    Identifier  "Millennium II"
    VendorName  "Unknown"
    BoardName   "Unknown"
    VideoRam    4096
EndSection


Section "Screen"
    Driver      "svga"
    Device      "Millennium II"
    Monitor     "DEC PCXBV-KA/KB"
    Subsection "Display"
        Depth       16
        Modes       "1280x1024"
        ViewPort    0 0
        Virtual     1280 1024
    EndSubsection
EndSection
------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Bye,
  Rob.



