I've managed to get RH6.0 to install on my Microway
PC164 system.  After installation I restarted and
booted milo.dd from the SRM.  At the milo prompt
I enter

MILO> boot sda2 linux

since my root partition is sda2 (marked active in
fdisk).  At this point the boot seems to start then
it prompts me to choose an "active configuration" or
something like that (looks kind of like the lilo
prompt) so I type "linux" since that is the only option
and hit enter and ... then ... nothing ...

It just sits there.  Not a bleepin' bleep.

Ok, so I had a problem with the ncr53c875 scsi controller
during the install but managed to tweak it to work
by telling the drive to work asynchronously with,

echo "setsync 0 255" > /proc/scsi/ncr53cxx/0

which worked wonders.  Anyone know if I can get
this to behave like this from the start?

