Milo and the kernel it was compiled against must match. once you have
milo booting, you can boot newer kernels with an older Milo. Just grab 
the sources and compile yourself a kernel. Place that kernel in the
same directory, where the older one is and create a new OS selection
in the BIOS. works fine for me. 

