I would advise AGAINST new owners immediately modifying the multia box.
First get it all together and run it completely tightly closed as it was
intended. Slight openings or modifications could change the whole intended
(engineered) airflow. Mine runs slightly warm but not hot. I'd say I
probably won't have a problem. Also .... use the stand for verticle mount
as the processor is near the top in this position and will ventilate more
quickly. (heat rises) But if all hope fails resort to the fan idea.
Remember lock the back closed and if no floppy make sure you have the
block installed in the floppy opening.
It almost seems like the operating temperature varies machine to machine
if everyone has taken these precautions?

