Thorsten Schlueter (thorsten.s@spans.de) wrote:

: The kernel starts and hangs (sometimes at eth0 init or somewhere else).

Did you try to start your machine in a single user mode?  Just add
'single' to your normal startup command.  If you get a shell then you
can figure out, step-by-step, which service gives you troubles and
correct your startup.  Quite likely you have a misconfigured network and
your system tries to get a response from DNS which never comes.  A
timeout on this is of an order of 20 minutes so probably your system
does not hang but is simply waiting.  Bad sendmail configuration is
famous for troubles of that sort.

'chkconfig' command provides an easy way to control what starts
and on what level.  A "multiuser console" is, for Red Hat, level 3
and xdm (gdm/kdm) starts on level 5.

   Michal



