Try to run OpenBSD, Linux is still to unstable for alpha machines (in my opinion)
OpenBSD is a true multi-platform unix, Linux not.

Linux is originally written for Intel machines (32 bits) the Alpha is 64 bits.
This generates problems for the c compiler.
Most things will work, but it is still not stable....
OpenBSD is multi-platform... so there are already 64 bits versions....
I run OpenBSD on axpci Alpha, it's extremely stable....
I installed linux on a lx machine, it is very unstable... redhat 6.0
If it is up it stays up, but rebooting isn't possible... you have to switch it
off and on.....
Some programs won't work... even you recompile them... so use OpenBSD instead
(This is my personally opinion, nothing wrong with Linux.. but for Alpha's it
is not good enough yet.)

You can find OpenBSD at http://www.openbsd.org 

