>Gustavo Yanes
>
>
I don't know if you got the sollution, so I mail it to you (because I
solved it this evening...)

* make a small DOS-partition (2Mb) (this is done automatically when
installing RH5.2)
* after the installation, boot once more from the MILO-floppy and
give, instead of 'boot fd0' 'boot hda5:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda5' (in
my case): the rest of the files should be loaded from the harddisk.
* leave the MILO-floppy in fd0 and, after login, give the command 'dd
if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/hda1 bs=1440k'. Milo and linload.exe are copied to
the DOS-partition hda1.

in the ARC bootmenu, 'add boot selection'; 'new system partition',
'IDE', osloader = \linload.exe, os in same partition as osloader, '\'
is os  rootdir; no debugger at boot time.

change boot selection: OSLOADFILENAME="\milo"; OSLOADOPTIONS= 
'boot hda5:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda5' (in my case).

(the longer story is in the 'Alpha Installation Addendum', 1.5.5)



