: > have to power off the machine.

: Sounds just like and IRQ conflict or the Sound card is taking
: the IRQ. I had a PCMCIA Interface slot card do this. 

Apparently some PCI soundcards cut in hardware IRQ assign lines to four
bits; Windoze will not use more so this is not a problem there.  The end
result is that a card gets assigned, say, IRQ 22 and is happily using
IRQ 6 instead.  PCI bus gets crazy and boom...  Count yourself lucky if
you did not "play" something into your SCSI controller and disks.
Anybody has any ideas how to work around this terminal stupidity?   From
what I hear this trend to a substandard broken hardware is actually
gaining a momentum.

  Michal




