Matti Kari (maza@surfhost.surfnet.fi) wrote:

: BTW., why not to use "make menuconfig"?

Because it is buggy and although it may work, sometimes, then you
may get nasty surprises on other ocassions.  The same applies to
'make xconfig', unfortunately.

Once you have .config and you want to do some adjustment in a safe
and fast way then edit out from .config **everything**  you want
to modify, "commented" or not, and run 'make oldconfig'.  You can
also copy that way .config from one kernel version to another but
do not forget to run 'make oldconfig' after 'cp'.  

This is also a method for fixing .config files mangled by "make
menuconfig" but you may need to go there with an editor first.

  Michal




