For the past several months I've been having problems with my lx164
machine.  The problems I have seen are:  SCSI probes failing, memory
checks failing, a black screen at power on, and the machine not being
able to boot from various drives.  When I have been able to get linux
to boot, the machine frequently crashes displaying a message along the
lines of:
"pyxis machine check vector=0x670 code=0x98 processor detected hard
error"

These problems happen frequently but at unpredictable times.

I have tried reloading the firmware and putting in a new power supply,
besides the usual reseating everything, but to no effect.  I also
tried underclocking the CPU.  I know that it's not a heat problem
because the machine will work fine one day, then fail to boot the next
(after having been off all night).  Then it will boot a few days later.

According to the ARM, this machine check indicates a problem with the
processor or on-chip caches (as opposed to memory or peripherals).  I
guess my question is, is it really possible that I have a faulty CPU
(as opposed to a faulty board/memory/scsi controller)?  I've never
seen a CPU fail when running at the appropriate clock rate, but I
guess there's a first time for everything.

Thanks for any advice.

Matt Grossman
