Sorry for the crosspost, but I think it's an important note.  Can't say
I recommend any 3Dfx based products as they are not forthcoming on any
3D implementation details.

I know that Permedia based cards have a solid reputation.  The Matrox
G200 card is also a good one, but not as 3D supported I believe.
nVidia cards never get BIOS initialized for me on alpha systems.

Metrolink is delivering an Extreme-3D driver supporting the following:
  E&S REALimage� 1000, 2100 (Evans & Sutherland,GLINT GMX� 1000, 2000, ,
MX, TX; and Permedia� 2, 3 (3Dlabs).

I would be weary of any implementation which doesn't provide 3D hardware
support.  I have been delving into the problem for about 3 months now,
and have found that if you want to do serious OpenGL, then alpha is not
a good solution now.  This is not to say that it won't be, however ;-)

Roger

