: Why?  Why the hell do you care so much?

Why do I care?  I thought that we had already established that I am a
shallow individual who is interested only in his rankings in the results
tables.  Obviously, I want a faster client so that I can move further up the
tables!

:>: Yes, but they want to have centralized control over verifying that clients
:>: perform as expected.  That means that they have one person whom they trust
:>: to do the verification, which is a good thing.
:>
:>This is not an issue with the Tru64 clients as outlined above.

: No it still may be an issue.  You don't understand how clients are developed
: by porters and how they're submitted to S@H.

Obviously not.  My thinking (and if this is wrong please provide a detailed
explanation of why) is that if a client has already been approved (and I
have just proved again why this must be true for the Tru64 clients) then it
doesn't need to be approved again and therefore any issue related to the
manpower required to approve it are irrelevant.  Are you suggesting that a
client is approved once to be run by the porter (no matter how many results
that port submits with it) and again before it can be released to everybody? 
Since the unreleased Tru64 clients have now turned out far more WUs that
many of the publically available clients for less popular platforms this
seems a slightly peculiar approach.

Perhaps you would care to educate us by outlining the exact procedure by
which clients are developed by porters and submitted to S@H.

:>: Yet Another Volunteer is probably not a good solution.
